The design of the segment-based capture buffer (data/SegmentRingBuffer.kt) is
derived from highlight-recorder, an independent GPL-3.0 project:

    highlight-recorder (https://github.com/owen88ob/highlight-recorder)
    Copyright (c) owen88ob
    Licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3

Specifically, this product adopts its approach of cutting the ring buffer at
actual key-frame boundaries so that a snapshot is decodable without a save-time
key-frame search, together with its soft/hard segment-length limits and forced
segmentation. The implementation here is a rewrite for this codebase: it uses
this project's millisecond monotonic clock and adds a byte budget to eviction.

